## 🎯 Safe Area Strategy (CRITICAL)

### Single Source of Truth
All safe area values are defined as CSS variables in `globals.css`:
```css
:root {
  /* Change fallback values HERE - they apply everywhere */
  --sai-top: env(safe-area-inset-top, 24px);
  --sai-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 28px);
  --sai-left: env(safe-area-inset-left, 0px);
  --sai-right: env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px);
  --sai-side-landscape: 24px;
}
```

### Rules:
1. **NEVER hardcode safe area values** in components - use `var(--sai-*)` or utility classes
2. **Use CSS classes** for positioning, not inline styles with env()
3. **Use `landscape:px-6`** for side padding in landscape mode (24px)
4. **Portrait**: Bottom safe area visible (28px)
5. **Landscape**: Bottom safe area = 0, side padding = 24px

### Fixed Elements Pattern:
```tsx
// Fixed header - NEEDS pt-safe class
<nav className="fixed top-0 w-full pt-safe">

// Fixed bottom nav - use CSS class for orientation-aware positioning
<nav className="fixed left-0 right-0 bottom-nav-position landscape:px-6">

// Page content - use flex-1 and overflow-y-auto
<div className="flex-1 overflow-y-auto landscape:px-6">
```

### AppShell Pattern:
All pages are wrapped in `AppShell` which handles safe areas:
```tsx
// In _app.tsx - already done, don't duplicate
<AppShell>
  <Component {...pageProps} />
</AppShell>
```

### Bottom Navigation Positioning:
Use the `bottom-nav-position` CSS class:
```css
.bottom-nav-position {
  bottom: var(--sai-bottom);  /* Portrait: 28px */
}
@media (orientation: landscape) {
  .bottom-nav-position {
    bottom: 0;  /* Landscape: no bottom gap */
  }
}
```

### DO NOT:
- ❌ Use `env(safe-area-inset-*, fallback)` directly in components
- ❌ Use inline styles for safe area positioning
- ❌ Add `min-h-screen` or `h-[100vh]` to page content (use `flex-1`)
- ❌ Hardcode pixel values for safe areas

### DO:
- ✅ Use `var(--sai-*)` CSS variables
- ✅ Use utility classes: `pt-safe`, `pb-safe`, `bottom-nav-position`
- ✅ Use `landscape:px-6` for consistent side padding
- ✅ Use `flex-1 overflow-y-auto` for scrollable content

---

## 📱 Mobile-First & Responsive Design (CRITICAL)

### Every Feature MUST Work in Both Orientations

Portrait and landscape have very different constraints:
- **Portrait**: Narrow but tall - stack vertically, scroll down
- **Landscape**: Wide but short - must keep buttons visible, content scrolls

### Landscape-Safe Modal Pattern:
```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - buttons get cut off in landscape
<div className="h-[500px]">
  <div>Content</div>
  <button>Save</button>  // User can't see this!
</div>

// ✅ CORRECT - scrollable body, fixed header/footer
<div className="max-h-[85vh] sm:max-h-[90vh] flex flex-col">
  <header className="flex-shrink-0 p-4">Title</header>
  <main className="flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-4">
    Scrollable content - can be any height
  </main>
  <footer className="flex-shrink-0 p-4">
    <button>Save</button>  // Always visible!
  </footer>
</div>
```

### Landscape-Specific Styles:
```tsx
// Use Tailwind's landscape: prefix
className="max-w-md landscape:max-w-2xl"      // Wider in landscape
className="py-4 landscape:py-2"                // Less vertical padding
className="block landscape:hidden"             // Hide in landscape
className="hidden landscape:block"             // Show only in landscape
className="min-h-[200px] landscape:min-h-0"   // Flexible height
```

### What to Hide/Show:
- **In landscape, HIDE**: Long descriptions, examples, hints
- **In landscape, KEEP**: Title, input fields, action buttons
- **In landscape, MAKE WIDER**: Modals, forms, content areas

### Breakpoints (Tailwind):
- `sm`: 640px (small tablets)
- `md`: 768px (tablets)
- `lg`: 1024px (desktop - hide mobile nav, show sidebar)
- `xl`: 1280px

### Landscape Detection:
```css
@media (orientation: landscape) { }
```
Or in Tailwind: `landscape:` prefix

### Bottom Navigation:
- Height: 64px (`h-16`)
- Use `bottom-nav-position` CSS class for positioning
- Add `landscape:px-6` for side padding in landscape
- Hidden on desktop: `lg:hidden`
```tsx
<nav className="fixed left-0 right-0 h-16 bottom-nav-position landscape:px-6 lg:hidden">
```

---

## 🌐 RTL Support (Arabic)

### Always use logical properties:
```tsx
// ✅ Good - works for RTL
className="ps-4 pe-2 ms-auto me-0"
className="text-start" // not text-left
className="rounded-s-lg" // not rounded-l-lg

// ❌ Bad - breaks RTL
className="pl-4 pr-2 ml-auto mr-0"
className="text-left"
```

### Direction attribute:
```tsx
<div dir={isRTL ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>
```

---

## 🧩 Component Patterns

### Page Layout:
```tsx
// Dashboard pages use DashboardLayout
export default function MyPage() {
  return (
    <DashboardLayout>
      {/* Content - no safe area classes needed */}
    </DashboardLayout>
  );
}
```

### Modals:
- Use the `Modal` component from `@/components/ui`
- Modals have automatic bottom safe area padding
- Portrait: Bottom sheet style
- Landscape: Centered modal

### Loading States:
- Use `PageSkeleton` for full-page loading
- Use `loading` prop on buttons
- Use `AppSkeleton` for app-level loading

---

## 🎨 Design Tokens

### Colors (Tailwind):
- `brand-*`: Primary green (#0D9488)
- `surface-*`: Grays for backgrounds/text
- `accent-*`: Orange highlights

### Fonts:
- Display: `font-display` (Outfit)
- Body: `font-sans` (DM Sans)
- Arabic: Cairo/Tajawal (auto-loaded)

